{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-88034",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "For similar polygons, the ratios of lengths of the corresponding sides should be the same.\n\n- Let's check option I:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{BC}{MN} & =\\frac{4}{2}=2, \\\\ \\frac{CA}{NL} & =\\frac{2}{1}=2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option I does give possible values of $MN$ and $NL.$\n\n- For option II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{BC}{MN} & =\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ \\frac{CA}{NL} & =\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option II does give possible values of $MN$ and $NL.$\n\n- For option III, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{BC}{MN} & =\\frac{4}{10}=\\frac{2}{5}, \\\\ \\frac{CA}{NL} & =\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option III does not give possible values of $MN$ and $NL.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
